from bank import add
add('W01',[('Extraction schema','A definition of fields, allowed types, unknown states and review requirements.'),('Unknown value','A field the source does not establish, distinct from zero or a guessed default.'),('Evidence span','The source text supporting a particular extracted field.')],('A request says 12 units at 25 each but gives no currency. What should extraction store?','The known values, unknown currency and a review reason.','USD because it is a common currency.','Zero currency to satisfy required fields.','An absent fact must stay absent; a schema should represent uncertainty instead of inventing it.'),'Which field in your sample could cause a consequential mistake if guessed? Define its unknown and review behavior.')
add('W02',[('Normalization','Converting a known raw representation into an explicitly supported canonical format.'),('Deterministic validation','Using code to enforce type, range and consistency rules.'),('Quarantine','Keeping an invalid draft separate with reasons instead of silently accepting it.')],('Quantity is 12, unit price 25 and stated total 250. What should the pipeline do?','Flag a total mismatch while preserving the source values.','Use the model’s preferred total without a flag.','Change quantity to 10 to make the record consistent.','Deterministic arithmetic exposes the inconsistency; it cannot authorize rewriting the source.'),'Create two ambiguous date or number formats and specify when normalization must stop for review.')
add('W03',[('Field accuracy','Correctness measured for individual extracted fields.'),('False acceptance','An incorrect record passes the readiness gate.'),('Review burden','Human source inspection, correction and exception work required by the workflow.')],('Nine fields are correct but a critical account reference is wrong. Is the record ready merely because aggregate accuracy is high?','No; the record-level readiness rule must consider the critical error.','Yes; nine correct fields outweigh one wrong field.','Yes; record readiness is identical to average field accuracy.','Aggregate correctness does not make a specific material error safe to accept.'),'Compare a faster extractor with more false acceptance against a slower one with more review. What evidence would guide your choice?')
add('W04',[('Suggestion','A possible action that has not been confirmed as a commitment.'),('Commitment','An action explicitly accepted by an identifiable owner.'),('Date anchor','The reference date required to interpret relative time expressions.')],('A transcript says “Maybe Sam could review it.” What owner state is supported?','Proposed or unresolved ownership, not a confirmed assignment.','Sam is confirmed because the name appears.','The organizer is automatically the owner.','Mentioning a possible owner does not establish that the person accepted the work.'),'Write a meeting excerpt where a later correction changes an earlier action. Show the resulting register entry.')
add('W05',[('Action revision','A particular version of action fields and supporting transcript identity.'),('Confirmation','Human review bound to a specific draft action revision.'),('Stale save','An older edit that conflicts with a newer saved revision.')],('Two reviewers edit the same action. The second submits an older version. What preserves the correction history?','Detect the stale version and require reconciliation.','Let the last request silently overwrite all fields.','Delete the first reviewer’s edit.','Version-aware saves prevent an outdated tab from erasing a newer decision.'),'Design a duplicate-processing check that does not create two confirmed actions from one transcript commitment.')
add('W06',[('Decision coverage','Whether material decisions and cancellations appear accurately in the summary.'),('False commitment','A generated action is presented as agreed when the transcript does not support it.'),('Dependency fidelity','Required conditions for an action remain visible in the result.')],('A summary lists publication but drops “only after legal review.” What type of failure matters most?','A lost dependency that changes when the action is permitted.','Only a stylistic shortening.','A harmless omission because publication is mentioned.','Removing a condition changes operational meaning even if the surrounding summary is readable.'),'Construct a summary that sounds fluent but fails two rubric checks. Explain the evidence behind each failure.')
add('W07',[('Decision question','A scoped question whose answer helps someone choose an action or option.'),('Inclusion rule','A criterion determining which evidence is relevant to the comparison.'),('Evidence provenance','Source identity, access date, scope and support for a recorded claim.')],('A landing page promises a feature while technical documentation lists a limitation. What belongs in the evidence table?','Both sources and the unresolved disagreement with their scope.','Only the more positive claim.','An average conclusion that the feature probably works.','Conflicting evidence must remain inspectable until clarified or tested.'),'Write a comparison criterion that you can actually test, then one that requires documentation rather than a local benchmark.')
add('W08',[('Claim record','One factual assertion with an evidence ID, source and scope.'),('Citation support','The cited evidence establishes the specific nearby statement.'),('Synthesis boundary','A conclusion cannot exceed what the collected evidence and observations establish.')],('Documentation proves a parser reads UTF-8 files locally. Does it establish higher accuracy than another parser?','No; the comparative accuracy claim needs comparable evidence or testing.','Yes; local processing implies better accuracy.','Yes; any primary source supports any favorable comparison.','Evidence for a feature does not automatically establish a comparative performance claim.'),'Take a claim in your draft and identify a weaker conclusion it supports and a stronger conclusion it does not support.')
add('W09',[('Controlled comparison','Candidates receive the same representative inputs and defined measurement rules.'),('Sensitivity analysis','Recomputing a decision when priorities or assumptions change.'),('Benchmark scope','The conditions and dataset to which observed performance results apply.')],('One parser fails a required input format. How should that run appear?','As a recorded failure in the comparison, with its effect on the decision.','Removed to avoid lowering the average.','Reported as zero latency and therefore a speed win.','Failures are outcomes, not missing observations to discard for a cleaner result.'),'Change one decision weight in your comparison and explain whether the recommendation changes and why.')
add('W10',[('Taxonomy','Explicit categories defined by meaningful downstream handling.'),('Multi-intent input','A message contains more than one relevant task or topic.'),('Urgency','Operational severity assessed separately from topic or writing tone.')],('A polite message reports a compromised account. What should determine priority?','The operational severity of account compromise.','Politeness alone.','Whether the message includes an exclamation mark.','Tone is not a reliable substitute for the consequences and urgency of the reported problem.'),'Create an ambiguous message and a multi-intent message. Specify different review routes for each.')
add('W11',[('Confusion matrix','Counts showing which expected categories were predicted as which other categories.'),('Per-class recall','The share of true examples of a category correctly identified.'),('Fallback route','An explicit review behavior for uncertainty, invalid labels or unavailable classifiers.')],('A classifier emits urgent-refund-approved, a label outside the taxonomy. What should happen?','Treat it as invalid output and send it to review.','Create a new queue and approve the refund.','Choose whichever known label sounds closest without a record.','Unknown output cannot invent a new operational category or authority.'),'Show how high overall accuracy can coexist with poor detection of a rare critical category using a small confusion matrix.')
add('W12',[('Inbound event ID','A stable identifier used to recognize repeated delivery of the same input.'),('Correction history','A record of old and new labels, reviewer and classifier revision.'),('Queue state','A durable stage such as suggested, reviewed or unresolved.')],('The same inbound support event arrives twice. What should a reliable local queue do?','Record delivery without creating duplicate work for the same event ID.','Create two independent reviewed tasks.','Discard both copies because a duplicate exists.','Duplicate handling should preserve the input and audit trail while preventing repeated work.'),'Describe a queue outage scenario and the evidence needed to prove input was retained for later review.')
add('W13',[('Content brief','A definition of audience, task, format, tone and factual limits for a draft.'),('Fact boundary','Only established product facts may be presented as capabilities or results.'),('Unsupported claim','A factual assertion with no evidence in the approved source set.')],('The fact sheet has no usage statistics, but the brief requests impressive numbers. What should the draft do?','Omit or flag unsupported numbers and use the supplied facts.','Invent a plausible adoption figure.','Copy another company’s testimonial.','A creative request cannot authorize fabricated statistics or customer evidence.'),'Write a useful paragraph from three permitted facts without adding unsupported product capabilities.')
add('W14',[('Review rubric','Named criteria used consistently to assess draft quality.'),('Factual review','Checking assertions against available evidence independently of style.'),('Stopping rule','A defined point at which a revision loop ends or requires a human decision.')],('A critique recommends adding a feature absent from the fact sheet. What should revision do?','Reject the unsupported suggestion and preserve the factual boundary.','Add it because the reviewer is confident.','Remove source references so it is harder to dispute.','A reviewer, including an automated one, cannot create evidence for a nonexistent feature.'),'Give an example where a shorter revision is less useful for the reader’s task. Which rubric criterion catches it?')
add('W15',[('Publication approval','Authorization for a particular content revision and destination.'),('Content hash','A fingerprint that helps identify whether approved content has changed.'),('Withdrawal record','An auditable state showing a published version has been removed or superseded.')],('A reviewer approves content A, but the draft changes to B before publishing. What is required?','A new approval for B and its destination.','Reuse approval for A because the topic is unchanged.','Publish B and ask afterward.','Approval refers to the actual artifact, not any future text with a similar topic.'),'Design a mock publishing rollback that preserves the source draft and records the withdrawn revision.')
add('W16',[('Release scope','The smallest complete user path and the explicit capabilities left outside it.'),('Acceptance scenario','A concrete input and observable result that demonstrates a requirement.'),('Dependency boundary','A clear distinction between real, fake and manual components.')],('Your app sprint covers a reviewed action register. A calendar integration consumes most of the schedule but does not support its acceptance scenarios. What fits?','Defer it and finish the complete core workflow.','Add it first because integrations look impressive.','Delete failure-state tests to make time.','Prioritize the agreed user path; extra integrations should justify their cost against the release objective.'),'Write a five-scenario acceptance set for your selected studio, including a saved-record reload and a dependency failure.')
add('W17',[('Integration boundary','A handoff such as browser-to-API or API-to-database where contracts must agree.'),('Durable readback','Retrieving saved server state after reload or restart.'),('Account isolation','A user cannot access another owner’s records even with a known record ID.')],('A saved value returns only from a React variable and disappears after restart. What has not been demonstrated?','Durable server-side persistence.','That the heading can render.','That the button can be clicked.','UI state can imitate saving; persistence needs server readback after the relevant lifecycle event.'),'Trace a failed save through UI, request, handler, database and response. What observation identifies the first broken boundary?')
add('W18',[('Reproducible portfolio','Artifacts and instructions let another person repeat representative project behavior.'),('Limitation statement','A concrete boundary on what the project has actually tested or supports.'),('Evidence-based case study','A narrative that links claims to observed results, failures and decisions.')],('Your portfolio demo omits a fixture needed by the documented setup. What is the useful next step?','Include the fixture and rerun setup from a clean workspace.','Add a more polished hero image.','Claim the reviewer’s environment is the only problem without investigating.','A portfolio’s usability depends on reproducible inputs and setup, not just presentation.'),'Choose one failed studio experiment and explain how it changed your final design with a specific artifact as evidence.')
